-- title:
--   Tame invariants: finite presentation, normality, flatness and smoothness descend
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a noetherian commutative domain, let $A$ and $B$ be commutative rings with $B$ a domain, equipped with $O$-algebra structures and an $A$-algebra structure on $B$ forming a scalar tower over $O$, with $B$ of finite type as an $O$-algebra; let $G$ be a finite group acting on $B$ by ring automorphisms commuting with the $O$-action, such that `IsGaloisGroup G A B` holds (so that $B$ is Galois over $A$ with group $G$, $A$ playing the role of the invariants) and the structure map $A \to B$ is injective (`FaithfulSMul A B`). Assume the image of $\#G$ in $O$ is a unit. Then: $A$ is of finite type and of finite presentation over $O$, and $B$ is a finite $A$-module; if $B$ is integrally closed then so is $A$; if $B$ is flat over $O$ then so is $A$; and for every ideal $\mathfrak a \subseteq O$, writing $\mathfrak a A$ and $\mathfrak a B$ for the ideals generated by the images of $\mathfrak a$, (i) an element of $A$ whose image lies in $\mathfrak a B$ already lies in $\mathfrak a A$, (ii) every $b \in B$ with $g \cdot b - b \in \mathfrak a B$ for all $g \in G$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak a B$ to the image of some $a \in A$, and (iii) for every $n$, if $B/\mathfrak a B$ has Krull dimension at most $n$ then so does $A/\mathfrak a A$. Finally, if $B$ is flat over $O$ and for every prime $\mathfrak p$ of $O$ the fibre $\mathfrak p$`.Fiber A` is formally smooth over the residue field of $\mathfrak p$, then $A$ is smooth over $O$.
--
--   This is the descent package for a tame quotient: the classical statements that the ring of invariants of a finite group acting on a finite-type algebra, with the group order invertible in the base, inherits finiteness, normality, flatness, fibrewise behaviour and (via the fibrewise criterion) smoothness. It is used in the construction of charts on modular curves, where rings of invariants of auxiliary level structures must be shown to be smooth over the base and to have controlled fibres.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsGaloisGroup_finitePresentation_and_smooth_invariants_typeZero_of_isUnit_natCard_of_smooth_fibers.lean

